  "term": "principle of economy",
  "definition": "In this historical aesthetic sense, the principle of economy is the view that something is beautiful or artistically effective when it contains only what is essential and leaves out anything unnecessary. It also came to be linked with the idea that what avoids wasted effort or energy can appear more graceful or pleasing.",
